-- title:
--   Patching descent at zero relation ideal: M free, kerψ=(φ(Xᵢ))
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring that is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring in Mathlib's sense, let $r\in\mathbb N$, let $R$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra and let $M$ be a nonzero $R$-module (all types in `Type`). Write $B=\mathcal O[[X_0,\dots,X_{r-1}]]$ for `MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪`. Suppose given a term `L` of the project's structure [`Algebra.PatchingLevel 𝒪 r R M ⊥`](def/Algebra_PatchingDatum.html#L5), i.e. at relation ideal $J=\bot$; unfolding the definition, this consists of: a $B$-module $N$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi$ of $B$; a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:B\to R$ with $\psi(\varphi(X_i))=0$ for every $i$; an additive surjection $\pi:N\to M$ satisfying $\pi(f\cdot x)=\psi(f)\cdot\pi(x)$ for all $f\in B$, $x\in N$, and whose kernel is exactly the submodule $\big(\varphi(X_0),\dots,\varphi(X_{r-1})\big)\cdot N$ (the ideal generated by the $\varphi(X_i)$ acting on all of $N$); and a natural number $d$ together with elements $b_0,\dots,b_{d-1}\in N$ such that every $x\in N$ can be written $\sum_i\varphi(c_i)\,b_i$ with $c_i\in B$, and $\sum_i\varphi(c_i)\,b_i=0$ holds if and only if every $c_i$ lies in $\bot$, i.e. every $c_i=0$. The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions: $M$ is a free $R$-module; the annihilator of $M$ in $R$ is the zero ideal; and $\ker\psi$ equals the ideal of $B$ generated by the set $\{\varphi(X_i):i\in\mathrm{Fin}\,r\}$ (so in particular $R\cong B/(\varphi(X_0),\dots,\varphi(X_{r-1}))$ through $\psi$). No completeness or finiteness hypothesis on $\mathcal O$, and no local or Noetherian hypothesis on $R$, is assumed.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra descent step at the end of the Taylor–Wiles patching argument, in the form given by Diamond (The Taylor–Wiles construction and multiplicity one, Thm. 2.1) and Fujiwara, cf. Darmon–Diamond–Taylor §5.9–5.10: a patched module that is free over a power-series ring acting through $\varphi$, with the expected kernel for $\pi$, forces freeness downstairs and realises $R$ as a quotient of $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$ by exactly $r$ elements. The formal statement concerns a single level of the project's [`Algebra.PatchingLevel`](def/Algebra_PatchingDatum.html#L5) data at relation ideal $\bot$ rather than an inverse system of levels, and the nontriviality of $M$ is an explicit hypothesis (it is used to produce a basis element of $N$ and hence the inclusion $\ker\psi\subseteq(\varphi(X_i))$). It is invoked in [`Algebra.PatchingDatum.bijective_and_free_of_surjective`](thm.html#Algebra.PatchingDatum.bijective_and_free_of_surjective), where the limit of a patching datum supplies such a level, and through it in the comparison of a deformation ring with a Hecke algebra for the Frey curve.
-- source:
